post_install() {
  cat >&2 <<'EOF'

fenrig-apparmor-profiles is experimental until tested on the target Plasma
machine. The pacman hook reloads policy only when AppArmor is active. Restart
Firefox and Thunderbird after the first successful load. A hook failure is
visible; protection is not silently unloaded.

To activate AppArmor, first inspect the current state:
  systemctl status apparmor.service
  cat /sys/kernel/security/lsm
  cat /proc/cmdline

On systemd systems, enable the loader after confirming the kernel has AppArmor:
  sudo systemctl enable --now apparmor.service

If `apparmor` is absent from `/sys/kernel/security/lsm`, add it to the
existing `lsm=` option in the relevant systemd-boot loader entry, preserving
the other configured LSMs, then reboot. Do not remove the existing entry or
rewrite boot configuration automatically. Verify after reboot with:
  cat /sys/kernel/security/lsm
  sudo aa-status

Current XanMod example (verify this still matches the machine): the running
kernel is 7.3.4-x64v3-xanmod1, AppArmor is absent from its active LSM list,
and the systemd-boot entry is `/boot/loader/entries/xanmod.conf`. Edit the
existing `options` line and append:
  lsm=landlock,lockdown,yama,integrity,apparmor,bpf
Then run:
  sudo systemctl enable --now apparmor.service
  sudo reboot
Do not replace the existing options line or remove its root, graphics, or
other kernel parameters. Confirm after reboot that `/sys/kernel/security/lsm`
contains `apparmor`.

See the package README and Arch AppArmor documentation for the target's exact
boot-entry layout and LSM ordering.

EOF
}
post_upgrade() { post_install; }
post_remove() {
  cat >&2 <<'EOF'

If profiles remain loaded after removal, remove them explicitly:
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-bwrap
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-firefox
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-thunderbird
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-clamav-native
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-clamav-quarantine-gui
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-clamav-scan-gui
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-clamav-scan-quarantine-helper
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-libreoffice
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-evince
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-gwenview
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-okular
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-ark
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-spectacle
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-chromium
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-chrome
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-wowup-cf
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-mumble
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-mpv
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-mpv-yt-dlp
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-lutris
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-electron
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-discord
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-steam
  sudo apparmor_parser -R /etc/apparmor.d/fenrig-wine

The apparmor package's original profile files remain untouched. To restore
their labels after removal, reload the originals that exist on the machine
explicitly:
  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/firefox
  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/thunderbird
  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/chromium
  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/chrome
  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/Discord
  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/steam
EOF
}
